1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:08,400
[A beautiful girl]

3
00:00:08,490 --> 00:00:13,370
[was born in the fall of a great harvest.]

4
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:15,660
[Her parents named her]

5
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:16,930
[Widawidan]

6
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:22,350
[to commemorate the god of harvest.]

7
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:26,830
[When she was 14,]

8
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:29,120
[a plague ravaged the village.]

9
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:32,380
[In order to save the villagers,]

10
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:36,780
[Widawidan made a wish to Kakarayan.]

11
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:38,360
[Therefore,]

12
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:40,960
[Widawidan met Kakarayan]

13
00:00:41,050 --> 00:00:44,210
[in her dream that night.]

14
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:46,280
[In her dream,]

15
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:54,950
[Kakarayan used lotus leaves
to hold water for her to drink.]

16
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:57,020
[When she woke up the next day,]

17
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:06,700
[the villagers who were sick started
to recover even without taking any medicine.]

18
00:01:06,830 --> 00:01:12,240
[But as the villagers
recovered one by one,]

19
00:01:12,370 --> 00:01:16,020
[Widawidan became haggard day by day.]

20
00:01:16,110 --> 00:01:17,650
[Then spring came.]

21
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:20,860
[The plague got even worse.]

22
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:25,530
[The number of recovering villagers]

23
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:28,170
[couldn't keep up with the ones
who were dying.]

24
00:01:28,260 --> 00:01:30,100
[One night,]

25
00:01:30,190 --> 00:01:33,759
[someone saw Widawidan]

26
00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:40,050
[feeding her own blood
to the sick villagers.]

27
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:44,009
[They found out the secret
behind the villagers' recovery.]

28
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:44,840
[The next day,]

29
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:49,420
[all the villagers who were infected
had been cured.]

30
00:01:49,509 --> 00:01:53,470
[But no one brought up]

31
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:56,110
[the name Widawidan ever again.]

32
00:01:56,190 --> 00:02:00,900
[It was as if the girl named Widawidan]

33
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:05,350
[had never existed.]

34
00:02:07,410 --> 00:02:08,470
Are you okay?

35
00:02:10,009 --> 00:02:12,250
We have to go back now. Hurry!

36
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,530
Wu Yi-han and Ting-yi are in the office.

37
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:14,720
Didn't you see?

38
00:02:14,810 --> 00:02:16,210
He obviously came for you.

39
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:17,450
I can't let you go back.

40
00:02:17,579 --> 00:02:20,310
We can't leave them like that. I...

41
00:02:23,030 --> 00:02:24,880
Tell me.

42
00:02:24,970 --> 00:02:26,640
Who am I?

43
00:02:28,310 --> 00:02:29,720
Why?

44
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:31,350
Why?

45
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:33,110
Why am I always alone?

46
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:36,320
Grandma!

47
00:02:36,410 --> 00:02:39,230
Why do you look like my grandma?

48
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:49,170
Why did you bring me here?

49
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,710
Take me back there!

50
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,070
Hsieh Tien-ti, calm down.

51
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:52,950
I know!

52
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,400
Do you know how dangerous that was?

53
00:02:54,490 --> 00:02:56,870
I know! Let me go back there!

54
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:59,240
Why did it become like my grandma?

55
00:02:59,329 --> 00:03:01,360
Please tell me.

56
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,160
My grandma will be fine, right?

57
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:05,140
My grandma is fine, right?

58
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:02,320
[Episode 10, Because I'm Almighty,
Thus I'm Powerless]

59
00:06:02,410 --> 00:06:05,530
[Emergency]

60
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:58,900
Miss, can I help you?

61
00:06:58,990 --> 00:06:59,830
Hi.

62
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,630
I'm Banai Bulang's family.

63
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:03,520
The hospital called and told me

64
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:05,640
that my grandma fainted near the station.

65
00:07:05,770 --> 00:07:07,920
I want to ask how she's doing.

66
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,420
If she was sent to us,

67
00:07:09,510 --> 00:07:11,400
she would've been moved
to the isolation ward.

68
00:07:11,530 --> 00:07:12,630
The patient's condition

69
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:13,780
is stable now.

70
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:15,400
If anything unexpected happens,

71
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:17,600
we will inform the family later.

72
00:07:17,690 --> 00:07:18,440
Can you tell me

73
00:07:18,570 --> 00:07:20,200
which room she is in?

74
00:07:20,290 --> 00:07:22,050
When can family members go in to see her?

75
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:24,200
No family members are allowed
to go in right now.

76
00:07:24,290 --> 00:07:25,960
All patients have to be quarantined

77
00:07:26,050 --> 00:07:26,890
due to the White Algae Disorder.

78
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:28,650
It's the hospital rule.

79
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,710
I'm sorry, but can I ask you a favor?

80
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:31,460
I'm really worried about my grandma

81
00:07:31,550 --> 00:07:33,570
-Miss.
-because...

82
00:07:33,659 --> 00:07:35,470
Everyone sitting here

83
00:07:35,550 --> 00:07:37,180
is worried about their family
as much as you are.

84
00:07:37,270 --> 00:07:39,159
You're not the only one.

85
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:43,560
We understand how family members feel.

86
00:07:43,650 --> 00:07:45,670
But this is the hospital rule.

87
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:47,350
Please cooperate.

88
00:08:40,669 --> 00:08:43,360
I know you can save my grandma.

89
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:25,460
[It's because you saw that I was alive]

90
00:09:25,550 --> 00:09:26,830
[in the Reflection of Time,]

91
00:09:26,910 --> 00:09:29,420
[you decided to let everyone die.]

92
00:09:33,070 --> 00:09:33,910
[If the people around me]

93
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,540
[disappear one by one]

94
00:09:35,670 --> 00:09:37,080
[and I'm the only one that's left,]

95
00:09:37,210 --> 00:09:38,880
[what's the point in living?]

96
00:10:12,850 --> 00:10:14,480
Grandma said

97
00:10:15,490 --> 00:10:18,830
that wine leads to the Kawas.

98
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,230
So this method

99
00:10:26,090 --> 00:10:27,810
should allow me to find you, right?

100
00:10:58,610 --> 00:10:59,530
Kakarayan.

101
00:11:03,010 --> 00:11:04,420
Can I just

102
00:11:05,910 --> 00:11:06,880
see you once?

103
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:14,580
You have restored 'Orad's powers.

104
00:11:14,710 --> 00:11:16,690
He is once again your messenger.

105
00:11:17,970 --> 00:11:19,590
I'm sure you have your reasons, right?

106
00:11:22,150 --> 00:11:24,480
I'm sure that not letting him do anything

107
00:11:25,450 --> 00:11:27,210
isn't it.

108
00:11:31,250 --> 00:11:32,310
Kakarayan.

109
00:11:38,690 --> 00:11:40,410
Let me find you.

110
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:51,230
♫ Come on, come on ♫

111
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:56,550
♫ Let me hear you ♫

112
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:12,700
♫ Come on, come on ♫

113
00:12:12,790 --> 00:12:17,410
♫ Let me see you ♫

114
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:37,340
♫ Come on, come on ♫

115
00:12:37,430 --> 00:12:39,800
[Tien-ti.]

116
00:12:39,890 --> 00:12:42,310
[Why can't I see Tien-ti?]

117
00:12:44,510 --> 00:12:46,800
[The Reflection of Time
of the doomsday has changed.]

118
00:12:50,230 --> 00:13:01,320
♫ Show yourself before me ♫

119
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:36,650
Tien-ti.

120
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:39,600
Hsieh Tien-ti.

121
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:47,870
Why are you here?

122
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:52,970
So...

123
00:13:54,070 --> 00:13:55,920
was that a dream?

124
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:58,210
I couldn't find Kakarayan.

125
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:05,560
I'm leaving.

126
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:07,360
Why are you leaving?

127
00:14:08,990 --> 00:14:10,220
Didn't you want to see me?

128
00:14:12,770 --> 00:14:13,700
I wasn't looking for you.

129
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:18,140
I'm the one you've been calling out to.

130
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:22,630
Kakarayan?

131
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:27,780
What?

132
00:14:29,050 --> 00:14:30,460
Stop fooling around, okay?

133
00:14:33,190 --> 00:14:35,040
It seems like appearing before you

134
00:14:35,170 --> 00:14:36,620
with a familiar face

135
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:38,250
got you flustered.

136
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,430
I'll change my appearance then.

137
00:14:45,110 --> 00:14:46,040
Let's see.

138
00:14:54,090 --> 00:14:57,390
What are you doing? I don't get it.

139
00:15:07,590 --> 00:15:08,390
Is this

140
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:10,810
better for you?

141
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:26,650
Hold on.

142
00:15:33,070 --> 00:15:34,080
You are...

143
00:15:34,170 --> 00:15:36,060
I'm the one you've been looking for.

144
00:15:36,190 --> 00:15:38,350
The beginning and the end of everything.

145
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:42,270
The one whom you said

146
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:45,570
was the greatest God in the world

147
00:15:45,650 --> 00:15:47,370
but had no sense of duty

148
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:50,670
and the most irresponsible, Kakarayan.

149
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:53,000
How did you know

150
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:55,950
I said that?

151
00:16:09,630 --> 00:16:11,700
Whether it is what you've said

152
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:13,770
or thought about,

153
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:16,720
as long as it's something
you want to tell me,

154
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:19,000
I'll remember everything clearly.

155
00:16:19,090 --> 00:16:20,280
Including now.

156
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:23,620
Now?

157
00:16:23,710 --> 00:16:24,280
Yes.

158
00:16:25,430 --> 00:16:28,380
Right now, you're telling yourself

159
00:16:28,950 --> 00:16:30,880
that if I'm really Kakarayan,

160
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:32,290
then as long as I want it,

161
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:33,830
your grandma will wake up.

162
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,370
I can also stop

163
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:38,010
that Papa' orip with the white footprints

164
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:39,990
and stop the world from ending.

165
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:40,740
Is that right?

166
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:52,130
Yes.

167
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:58,250
If you really are Kakarayan,

168
00:16:59,350 --> 00:17:01,330
as long as you're willing to stop this,

169
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:03,570
I'm willing

170
00:17:03,710 --> 00:17:04,190
to do...

171
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:04,980
Whatever it takes.

172
00:17:11,579 --> 00:17:14,349
Just like what you did to 'Orad.

173
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:17,040
Whatever you need me to do,

174
00:17:17,130 --> 00:17:18,670
as long as you're willing to stop this,

175
00:17:19,630 --> 00:17:21,310
I'll surely do it.

176
00:17:28,390 --> 00:17:30,460
Are you trying to make a deal?

177
00:17:37,590 --> 00:17:42,120
I know it's rude of me to say this.

178
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:45,510
But based on my experience,

179
00:17:45,990 --> 00:17:48,940
there's always a price to pay

180
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:53,250
no matter which God you're praying to.

181
00:17:59,010 --> 00:18:00,200
You seek for me

182
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:02,710
because to you,

183
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:04,690
not only do I have everything,

184
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,450
but I can also do anything.

185
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,580
But have you thought about this?

186
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,500
If I have everything,

187
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:16,880
what else can you give me

188
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:17,890
that I don't already have?

189
00:18:18,990 --> 00:18:20,440
If I can do anything,

190
00:18:21,580 --> 00:18:22,950
what can you do for me

191
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:24,880
that I can't accomplish myself?

192
00:18:26,950 --> 00:18:28,180
For humans,

193
00:18:28,670 --> 00:18:29,500
paying the price

194
00:18:29,590 --> 00:18:31,620
and making such deals over and over

195
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:33,950
to get something in return

196
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:36,680
seem to be the only way
to keep the world running.

197
00:18:38,610 --> 00:18:40,280
But you've never thought of this.

198
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,640
Who was the one

199
00:18:45,390 --> 00:18:47,370
who made you pay the initial price?

200
00:18:49,430 --> 00:18:51,680
Whom did you make the deal with?

201
00:19:07,430 --> 00:19:08,220
Perhaps...

202
00:19:08,970 --> 00:19:10,110
from the very beginning,

203
00:19:11,130 --> 00:19:13,190
when humans didn't have
to pay for anything,

204
00:19:14,910 --> 00:19:17,070
I had already given you the world.

205
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:20,980
You just failed
to appreciate the blessings.

206
00:19:21,070 --> 00:19:22,830
[You used these blessings]

207
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:24,590
[as stakes for what you wish for.]

208
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:29,610
[But in return,]

209
00:19:29,690 --> 00:19:32,470
[did you really get what you wanted?]

210
00:19:34,970 --> 00:19:36,160
[When you were begging me to stop]

211
00:19:36,250 --> 00:19:37,790
[the Papa' orip with the white footprints]

212
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,470
[from hurting humans,]

213
00:19:40,870 --> 00:19:42,580
[have you thought about]

214
00:19:42,670 --> 00:19:44,390
[where he came from]

215
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:46,500
[and why he wanted to hurt you?]

216
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,820
Look at this stream.
Why has it turned into this color?

217
00:19:54,950 --> 00:19:57,020
I brought some kids over this morning

218
00:19:57,150 --> 00:19:59,350
and we were shocked to see it.

219
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:01,060
There's a factory upstream.

220
00:20:01,150 --> 00:20:03,040
They often drain the wastewater
when it's raining to cover it up.

221
00:20:03,130 --> 00:20:05,240
[Have you thought about it?]

222
00:20:05,990 --> 00:20:07,710
[Maybe before you begged me,]

223
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:08,810
[other living beings]

224
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:10,440
[had asked me to stop humans]

225
00:20:10,520 --> 00:20:12,020
[from hurting them.]

226
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:03,890
Toem.

227
00:21:06,230 --> 00:21:08,290
You're the goddess of clouds.

228
00:21:10,010 --> 00:21:11,370
Tell me.

229
00:21:12,430 --> 00:21:14,760
When a lie is exposed,

230
00:21:16,740 --> 00:21:18,240
what will happen to that lie?

231
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:38,870
Don't worry.

232
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:41,420
I didn't come here to hurt her.

233
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:42,880
On the contrary,

234
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,810
I'm here to help you find her.

235
00:22:05,010 --> 00:22:07,160
[You showed me all of this]

236
00:22:08,260 --> 00:22:09,760
to tell me

237
00:22:10,290 --> 00:22:11,340
that whatever is happening now

238
00:22:11,430 --> 00:22:13,240
is the product of our own actions.

239
00:22:15,260 --> 00:22:18,160
Are you saying
you won't accept my request?

240
00:22:19,130 --> 00:22:20,670
I just want you to know

241
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:23,750
that you don't have
to make a deal with me.

242
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:26,480
Because right from the start,

243
00:22:27,050 --> 00:22:28,590
I've given you

244
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:30,260
everything you need.

245
00:22:32,240 --> 00:22:33,470
The one who needs to make a choice

246
00:22:34,270 --> 00:22:36,550
is you, not me.

247
00:22:37,570 --> 00:22:40,160
But all the Kawas told me

248
00:22:40,950 --> 00:22:43,420
that you were the one
who arranged everything.

249
00:22:43,550 --> 00:22:45,090
Doesn't that mean

250
00:22:45,220 --> 00:22:47,470
whatever happens in this world

251
00:22:47,550 --> 00:22:49,970
is up to your choice?

252
00:22:53,670 --> 00:22:55,390
I can make a choice indeed.

253
00:22:57,980 --> 00:22:59,740
But what if the choice I make

254
00:23:00,890 --> 00:23:02,030
isn't what you want?

255
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:04,450
What do you mean?

256
00:23:05,990 --> 00:23:07,530
You want me to save your grandma

257
00:23:08,010 --> 00:23:08,670
and make the Papa' orip

258
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:11,180
with the white footprints disappear.

259
00:23:11,270 --> 00:23:12,500
Those are the choices you want me to make.

260
00:23:13,430 --> 00:23:14,610
In this world,

261
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:17,340
what should disappear

262
00:23:18,310 --> 00:23:19,810
and what can stay?

263
00:23:22,930 --> 00:23:25,170
If I decided that the ones to stay

264
00:23:25,350 --> 00:23:26,540
aren't the humans,

265
00:23:27,770 --> 00:23:29,090
will you still ask me to choose?

266
00:23:35,290 --> 00:23:37,800
So you're just going to let it be

267
00:23:37,890 --> 00:23:39,210
and do nothing?

268
00:23:41,280 --> 00:23:42,380
But you have the ability

269
00:23:42,510 --> 00:23:45,410
to change everything, don't you?

270
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:48,180
Yes.

271
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:53,240
It's because I'm almighty,

272
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:56,060
I'm powerless.

273
00:24:16,340 --> 00:24:18,280
Since I'm powerless,

274
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:22,150
I'm giving you my blessing.

275
00:24:30,290 --> 00:24:32,710
But to some people,

276
00:24:32,800 --> 00:24:34,470
that blessing is more of a curse.

277
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:43,530
Tien-ti.

278
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:48,370
Tien-ti, are you okay?

279
00:24:50,050 --> 00:24:51,720
Why did you pass out
at a convenience store?

280
00:24:53,350 --> 00:24:54,620
Why couldn't I sense you?

281
00:25:09,980 --> 00:25:10,860
Tien-ti.

282
00:25:13,630 --> 00:25:14,420
Hsieh Tien-ti.

283
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:19,480
Hsieh Tien-ti.

284
00:25:33,120 --> 00:25:34,840
[I met Kakarayan.]

285
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:37,080
Kakarayan?

286
00:25:40,290 --> 00:25:41,920
In order to save my grandma,

287
00:25:44,030 --> 00:25:45,880
I tried to summon Him.

288
00:25:46,940 --> 00:25:48,780
And I saw Him.

289
00:25:51,910 --> 00:25:54,110
I begged Him to reconsider

290
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:56,790
and stop all this from happening.

291
00:25:58,550 --> 00:25:59,560
Then...

292
00:26:01,280 --> 00:26:03,790
he rejected me.

293
00:26:06,120 --> 00:26:07,220
He showed me a lot of things

294
00:26:07,350 --> 00:26:09,600
I hadn't seen before.

295
00:26:10,170 --> 00:26:12,320
He told me things

296
00:26:12,940 --> 00:26:14,870
I didn't really understand.

297
00:26:16,550 --> 00:26:17,560
Something about

298
00:26:18,390 --> 00:26:23,320
me being the one
to make a choice and not him.

299
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:27,810
When I wanted to ask him

300
00:26:27,900 --> 00:26:29,090
what he meant,

301
00:26:29,170 --> 00:26:31,330
the red-eyed woman appeared.

302
00:26:31,420 --> 00:26:33,130
The red-eyed woman?

303
00:26:33,220 --> 00:26:34,410
Do you mean Toem?

304
00:26:34,500 --> 00:26:35,770
Yes, it's her.

305
00:26:36,480 --> 00:26:38,460
While Kakarayan was speaking to me,

306
00:26:38,590 --> 00:26:40,530
the red-eyed woman appeared.

307
00:26:40,660 --> 00:26:41,930
Did she do anything to you?

308
00:26:42,020 --> 00:26:43,030
Did she hurt you?

309
00:26:43,690 --> 00:26:44,350
No.

310
00:26:45,890 --> 00:26:46,730
But...

311
00:26:49,410 --> 00:26:50,870
she...

312
00:26:51,970 --> 00:26:53,550
killed Kakarayan in front of me.

313
00:27:14,050 --> 00:27:14,620
When you go back,

314
00:27:14,710 --> 00:27:17,130
tell him I'm sorry.

315
00:27:22,900 --> 00:27:25,400
She killed Kakarayan?

316
00:27:28,260 --> 00:27:29,890
And she wanted me

317
00:27:31,120 --> 00:27:33,150
to tell you she's sorry.

318
00:27:37,020 --> 00:27:38,690
Then I came back here.

319
00:27:43,050 --> 00:27:44,760
Why would

320
00:27:45,120 --> 00:27:46,170
that red-eyed woman appear?

321
00:27:46,610 --> 00:27:48,720
Why would she kill Kakarayan?

322
00:27:49,780 --> 00:27:52,380
Will Kakarayan die because of that?

323
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:54,400
What...

324
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:56,860
What's going on?

325
00:28:26,030 --> 00:28:28,760
She killed Kakarayan?

326
00:28:30,610 --> 00:28:32,240
And she wanted me

327
00:28:33,560 --> 00:28:35,710
to tell you she's sorry.

328
00:28:38,750 --> 00:28:39,540
I'm sorry.

329
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:49,790
This is the last time I'm lying to you.

330
00:30:10,490 --> 00:30:11,280
What happened?

331
00:30:19,810 --> 00:30:21,350
[I can make a choice indeed.]

332
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:26,190
But what if the choice I make

333
00:30:27,780 --> 00:30:29,050
isn't what you want?

334
00:30:40,140 --> 00:30:41,150
Hello?

335
00:30:42,910 --> 00:30:44,060
Yes, I'm Ms. Hsieh.

336
00:30:46,430 --> 00:30:48,060
Yes, I'm her family member.

337
00:31:06,760 --> 00:31:07,460
Doctor.

338
00:31:08,210 --> 00:31:10,680
Where's the doctor?

339
00:31:10,760 --> 00:31:12,220
I'm Banai Bulang's family.

340
00:31:12,300 --> 00:31:13,840
Are you Ms. Hsieh?

341
00:31:13,930 --> 00:31:15,340
Yes, she's my grandma.

342
00:31:15,430 --> 00:31:16,970
I was told

343
00:31:17,100 --> 00:31:18,110
that she was in critical condition.

344
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:18,990
How is she now?

345
00:31:19,430 --> 00:31:21,020
Since being admitted,

346
00:31:21,100 --> 00:31:23,300
the patient's Glasgow Coma Scale score
hasn't improved.

347
00:31:23,830 --> 00:31:25,500
Yesterday, she had severe sepsis

348
00:31:25,640 --> 00:31:27,220
and multiple organ failure.

349
00:31:27,310 --> 00:31:28,850
We took a CT scan just now

350
00:31:28,940 --> 00:31:31,490
and found that all her organs

351
00:31:31,580 --> 00:31:32,980
are covered in whitish algae.

352
00:31:39,060 --> 00:31:40,640
Are you saying

353
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:45,920
that my grandma

354
00:31:47,280 --> 00:31:48,380
most likely won't recover?

355
00:31:51,950 --> 00:31:52,960
Ms. Hsieh.

356
00:31:53,880 --> 00:31:55,380
We have to assume the worst.

357
00:31:55,990 --> 00:31:57,010
Your grandma

358
00:31:58,990 --> 00:32:00,570
might not live through the day.

359
00:32:06,950 --> 00:32:08,620
In that case...

360
00:32:08,750 --> 00:32:09,850
Doctor, please.

361
00:32:09,940 --> 00:32:11,480
Please, just this once.

362
00:32:11,610 --> 00:32:13,860
Let me see my grandma today.

363
00:32:15,970 --> 00:32:17,470
It has already come to this.

364
00:32:17,600 --> 00:32:19,580
Can't I see her even once?

365
00:32:20,190 --> 00:32:20,900
If my grandma

366
00:32:21,030 --> 00:32:22,390
can't make it past today,

367
00:32:22,480 --> 00:32:23,320
she won't have anyone

368
00:32:23,410 --> 00:32:25,170
next to her.

369
00:32:25,250 --> 00:32:26,090
Ms. Hsieh.

370
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:26,710
Please, I beg you.

371
00:32:26,790 --> 00:32:30,580
It's the hospital rule. I'm sorry.

372
00:32:30,670 --> 00:32:32,470
There's nothing we can do.

373
00:33:16,380 --> 00:33:17,040
Come on.

374
00:33:19,150 --> 00:33:20,430
I'll take you to her.

375
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:17,489
Grandma.

376
00:34:49,960 --> 00:34:54,540
♫ Come on, come on ♫

377
00:34:54,630 --> 00:34:58,410
♫ Let me hear you ♫

378
00:34:58,500 --> 00:35:01,360
♫ Come on, come on ♫

379
00:35:01,450 --> 00:35:05,190
♫ Let me see you ♫

380
00:35:05,280 --> 00:35:08,880
♫ Come on, come on ♫

381
00:35:08,970 --> 00:35:12,890
♫ Right at this moment ♫

382
00:35:12,980 --> 00:35:18,340
♫ Show yourself before me ♫

383
00:35:52,530 --> 00:35:54,110
Grandma.
